# ── blast25 streaming renderer ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# [2026-10-27 PDT] blast25: live append (rev6). Frames on stdin, NUL-separated:
#   B header ts_display iso   open a row (written at once: header first, output streams in)
#   C bytes                   output bytes for the open row (appended as they arrive)
#   E                         close the open row
#   X rc                      exit code of the command whose rows were opened since the last X
#   S                         sync: reply on stdout with "P <path>" per part opened since the last sync, then "K"
#   Q                         finish now (exit), reply "D <entries>\t<html>\t<json>"
# The renderer never prints to the terminal; blast prints its own lines (-> path, saved ...) in blast24's places.
# [2026-10-27 PDT] t83u blast25s ROTATION: before a row, rotate once the open part's real bytes reach the
# target (20 MB). While a row streams, the next piece of output (pieces end at a line break) that would push
# the open part past the hard cap (target + 50% = 30 MB) splits the row there: the row and the part are closed,
# and the same row (same id, time and header) continues in the next part. No part passes 30 MB. A row whose
# header is in the part but has no output there yet is moved whole instead (no empty row is left behind).
